  "interpretation": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Clinical Utility:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"913\" data-end=\"1025\">\n<p data-start=\"915\" data-end=\"1025\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">C4d IHC is used <strong data-start=\"931\" data-end=\"973\">primarily in renal transplant biopsies</strong> to detect <strong data-start=\"984\" data-end=\"1022\">antibody-mediated rejection (ABMR)</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1026\" data-end=\"1153\">\n<p data-start=\"1028\" data-end=\"1153\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1028\" data-end=\"1056\">Positive linear staining</strong> of peritubular capillaries indicates <strong data-start=\"1094\" data-end=\"1152\">complement activation due to donor-specific antibodies</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
